{
  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration found is config_035 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy. The data clearly shows scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000/scgpt for RNA, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50 for image, and multiprofile >> singleprofile. No untested configuration replicates the full optimal combination. Among untested configs, config_022 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) has the highest expected accuracy (~0.64-0.66) because it retains the best RNA encoder, best aggregation, and best fusion—only the image encoder is downgraded. This experiment tests whether the transformer+weighted aggregation/fusion combination generalizes across image encoders, confirming that the imagenet_vit_l encoder is the primary driver of the performance gap (config_011 with resnet50+avgpool+concat gave 0.6315, and the encoder swap to imagenet_vit_l contributed ~0.09 of the total gain to 0.725). As the final experiment, it cannot beat config_035 but provides the strongest confirmation of the design hierarchy. Expected cost: moderate-to-high (~5-7 GPU hours) due to multiprofile processing with transformer aggregation, comparable to config_011 (7.27) but potentially lower since transformer aggregation over resnet50 features may be less expensive than avgpool over the same."
}

